# Zanini Renovations — Project Rules

## Mobile-first responsive design (mandatory)

All present and future UI work — admin panel pages, components, partials, and
public site sections — MUST be designed mobile-first:

1. Design and implement the small-viewport (≤480px phone, ≤900px admin drawer
   breakpoint) layout FIRST, then progressively enhance for tablet/desktop
   with `min-width` media queries. Do not build desktop-only and "fix" mobile
   later.
2. Every new table must be wrapped in `.admin-table-scroll` inside an
   `.admin-card` (see `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` §4) — never a bare
   `.admin-table-wrap` without the scroll behavior. For data-dense tables,
   consider a stacked card layout below 640px instead of relying solely on
   horizontal scroll.
3. All interactive controls (buttons, tabs, checkboxes) must meet the 44px
   minimum touch target already mandated in `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` §1.5 and
   `.cursor/rules/admin-button-field-sizing.mdc`.
4. Any drag-and-drop or canvas-based interaction must support touch events
   (`touchstart`/`touchmove`/`touchend` or a pointer-events abstraction), not
   HTML5 `dragstart`/`dragover` alone.
5. Reuse the documented breakpoints in `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` §5
   (900 / 700 / 768px) instead of introducing new one-off breakpoints per
   page.
6. Before marking any UI task complete, verify the layout at a phone-width
   viewport (~375-414px) in addition to desktop.

## Admin light and dark themes (mandatory)

All present and future **authenticated admin** UI MUST work in both light and
dark mode, even when the user does not mention theme. Use `var(--admin-*)`
tokens; put leftover dark overrides in `public/css/admin-dark.css` scoped to
`html.admin-dark`. Public pages, PDFs, emails, and the login screen stay light
only — never leak dark styles into shared public CSS.

See `.cursor/rules/admin-light-dark.mdc`.

See `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` and `.cursor/rules/admin-layout-compact.mdc` /
`admin-button-field-sizing.mdc` for full detail — this file is the
top-level mandate; those files are the implementation reference.
